Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.30,0:00:07.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi everyone! This is GlycoTwin, my project for personalized\Npost-meal glucose modelling.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.93,0:00:15.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me show you how it works, what makes it different, and\Nthe research behind it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.15,0:00:20.82,Default,,0,0,0,,The big idea is that a forecast shouldn't be a one-off.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.86,0:00:26.04,Default,,0,0,0,,After the same meal, two people can respond very\Ndifferently,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.08,0:00:31.09,Default,,0,0,0,,so each twin here holds a personal estimate of how strongly
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.13,0:00:35.63,Default,,0,0,0,,that person's glucose rises per gram of carbohydrate.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.66,0:00:43.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Every forecast carries its own uncertainty, and every update\Ncreates a new, auditable version.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.81,0:00:48.67,Default,,0,0,0,,This section is the whole story in five steps.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.71,0:00:52.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Real data from the CGMacros research dataset.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.53,0:00:59.87,Default,,0,0,0,,A simple model: the rise in glucose is a personal\Nsensitivity, plus an activity effect,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.90,0:01:02.57,Default,,0,0,0,,times the grams of carbohydrate.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.62,0:01:06.23,Default,,0,0,0,,A forecast of the two-hour glucose maximum.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.26,0:01:09.95,Default,,0,0,0,,An observation, once that window has closed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.99,0:01:15.04,Default,,0,0,0,,And a Bayesian update that writes a new version of the twin.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.08,0:01:20.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Forecast, observe, update is the loop this project is built\Naround.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.59,0:01:26.54,Default,,0,0,0,,The research summary is honest too.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.58,0:01:35.84,Default,,0,0,0,,The first comparison of two model variants was inconclusive,\Nand I'll show you exactly what that means later.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.88,0:01:39.17,Default,,0,0,0,,But first, let me open the application.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.31,0:01:42.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll create an account first.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.72,0:01:48.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Each twin belongs to the person who created it, passwords\Nare hashed,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.44,0:01:54.20,Default,,0,0,0,,and the browser only keeps a session cookie, so I won't\Ndwell on that.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.24,0:02:01.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm using a throw-away email on a temporary database, so\Nnothing here touches real data.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.58,0:02:18.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I can create a Digital Twin.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.36,0:02:27.62,Default,,0,0,0,,For this walkthrough it starts from the built-in\Ndemonstration prior, which the interface labels synthetic,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.66,0:02:33.18,Default,,0,0,0,,because participant-level CGMacros data can't be shown\Npublicly.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.22,0:02:40.57,Default,,0,0,0,,The application can also load an aggregate prior exported\Nfrom the research pipeline.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.71,0:02:46.16,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the twin's state at version zero.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.20,0:02:57.45,Default,,0,0,0,,For Model B, the personal carbohydrate sensitivity, beta,\Nstarts at 0.747 with an uncertainty of 0.187.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.48,0:03:00.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Model C adds an activity term.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.77,0:03:05.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Every update will appear here as a new version.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.02,0:03:09.70,Default,,0,0,0,,The other pages follow the loop.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.74,0:03:13.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Forecast takes a meal and gives a forecast.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.40,0:03:18.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Observations is where an outcome is recorded and applied.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.24,0:03:26.02,Default,,0,0,0,,History lists every forecast and every version, and Insights\Ncompares forecast with outcome.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.06,0:03:27.89,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll use all of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.80,0:03:42.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Before the demo, a quick look at how it fits together.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.58,0:03:51.65,Default,,0,0,0,,The browser talks to a FastAPI back end, which stores\Naccounts, twins and every twin version in SQLite.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.69,0:03:56.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Behind it is the research engine, with Models B and C,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.46,0:04:04.38,Default,,0,0,0,,and the live twin uses the same update and forecast\Nfunctions as the research experiments.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.53,0:04:14.87,Default,,0,0,0,,The CGMacros pipeline that processes the real data runs\Noffline, on the researcher's own machine.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.91,0:04:21.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Only aggregate priors and reports ever cross over to the\Nwebsite.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.50,0:04:26.41,Default,,0,0,0,,So what's the research behind it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.45,0:04:33.03,Default,,0,0,0,,We use the CGMacros dataset: forty-five participants, about\Nten days each,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.06,0:04:40.80,Default,,0,0,0,,with minute-level glucose from two sensors, plus activity,\Nheart rate and logged meals.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.84,0:04:46.34,Default,,0,0,0,,It's released under a Creative Commons non-commercial\Nlicence.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.49,0:04:51.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Each meal is anchored at its logged meal row,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.18,0:04:59.26,Default,,0,0,0,,and the target is whether the maximum glucose in the next\Ntwo hours reaches one hundred and eighty.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.30,0:05:02.38,Default,,0,0,0,,That's exactly what the app forecasts.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.41,0:05:09.34,Default,,0,0,0,,One caveat: the dataset has no meal-end time, so we always\Nsay after the logged meal,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.38,0:05:11.96,Default,,0,0,0,,never after the end of the meal.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.11,0:05:20.49,Default,,0,0,0,,A meal is only used if its window has enough readings,\Nmissing glucose is never filled in,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.53,0:05:23.62,Default,,0,0,0,,and the main set keeps isolated meals.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.66,0:05:30.63,Default,,0,0,0,,On the Libre sensor that left one thousand, two hundred and\Nsixty-two eligible meals,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.66,0:05:33.83,Default,,0,0,0,,three hundred and one of them positive.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.88,0:05:37.47,Default,,0,0,0,,The Dexcom sensor is a sensitivity analysis,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.51,0:05:43.82,Default,,0,0,0,,because the two disagree on the label about twenty-three\Npercent of the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.96,0:05:53.84,Default,,0,0,0,,To avoid leakage, features only use information from before\Nthe meal, the folds are split by participant,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.87,0:06:01.22,Default,,0,0,0,,and evaluation is sequential, so a forecast only sees\Noutcomes that were already known.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.26,0:06:07.51,Default,,0,0,0,,The leakage check passed for all forty-five participants, on\Nboth sensors.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.86,0:06:12.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Now the main demonstration.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.35,0:06:22.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll enter one meal by hand: sixty grams of carbohydrate, an\Nactivity of 0.3 on the twin's zero-to-one scale,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.43,0:06:31.26,Default,,0,0,0,,and a pre-meal glucose of one hundred and ten, for the first\Nof January at eight in the morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.40,0:06:40.71,Default,,0,0,0,,And here's the forecast, made from version zero, before the\Ntwin has learned anything about this person.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.74,0:06:46.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Model B expects the two-hour maximum to be about one hundred\Nand fifty-five,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.84,0:06:54.34,Default,,0,0,0,,with a ninety percent interval from one hundred and\Ntwenty-six to one hundred and eighty-four,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.38,0:07:00.28,Default,,0,0,0,,and a seven point seven percent chance of reaching one\Nhundred and eighty.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.43,0:07:07.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Two hours later the window has closed, so I can record what\Nhappened.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.42,0:07:11.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll enter a maximum of one hundred and eighty-five.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.94,0:07:18.24,Default,,0,0,0,,That's a demonstration value I typed in, not a participant's\Nobservation.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.27,0:07:22.48,Default,,0,0,0,,The app only accepts it after the full two hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.64,0:07:27.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Recording it doesn't change the twin yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.14,0:07:35.31,Default,,0,0,0,,It waits until I apply it, and a meal with an unusable\Nwindow would be excluded instead of used.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.45,0:07:40.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I apply it. That creates version one.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.99,0:07:54.26,Default,,0,0,0,,On My Twin, beta has moved from 0.747 to 0.950, and its\Nuncertainty has shrunk from 0.187 to 0.144.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.30,0:08:01.57,Default,,0,0,0,,The twin is more certain, which isn't the same as more\Naccurate.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.62,0:08:08.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Both versions are in the history, and nothing was\Noverwritten.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.80,0:08:18.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Now the interesting part. Same meal, same activity, same\Nglucose, but a forecast at noon, made from version one.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.59,0:08:22.94,Default,,0,0,0,,The expected maximum is now one hundred and sixty-seven,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.98,0:08:28.90,Default,,0,0,0,,the interval runs from one hundred and forty to one hundred\Nand ninety-four,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.94,0:08:37.06,Default,,0,0,0,,and the chance of reaching one hundred and eighty has gone\Nfrom seven point seven to twenty-one percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.10,0:08:44.28,Default,,0,0,0,,The inputs are the same, but the twin's state has changed,\Nso its next forecast changes too.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.63,0:08:50.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's look at what the forecast really says.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.31,0:08:57.97,Default,,0,0,0,,The target is the maximum glucose in the two hours after the\Nmeal, not a full glucose curve,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.02,0:09:03.42,Default,,0,0,0,,so I'm not drawing one. The band is an interval for that\Nmaximum.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.57,0:09:09.03,Default,,0,0,0,,The curve on the right is the predictive distribution,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.07,0:09:14.54,Default,,0,0,0,,and the shaded part above one eighty is the threshold\Nprobability.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.58,0:09:20.80,Default,,0,0,0,,The table gives each model's mean rise, spread and ninety\Npercent interval.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.83,0:09:28.80,Default,,0,0,0,,That interval isn't a guarantee, and a note warns that the\Ntwin has little personal history yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.84,0:09:33.22,Default,,0,0,0,,GlycoTwin shows its uncertainty instead of hiding it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.24,0:09:38.07,Default,,0,0,0,,So how does Model B personalize?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.12,0:09:46.79,Default,,0,0,0,,The rise in glucose is a personal sensitivity, beta, times\Nthe grams of carbohydrate, plus noise.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.82,0:09:51.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Beta starts from a prior fitted on other participants,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.67,0:09:58.00,Default,,0,0,0,,and after each eligible observation a closed-form Bayesian\Nupdate moves
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.05,0:10:04.11,Default,,0,0,0,,its mean toward what that meal suggests and narrows its\Nuncertainty.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.25,0:10:09.66,Default,,0,0,0,,The forecast then comes straight from that current beta.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.70,0:10:17.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Only eligible outcomes can update the twin: the window must\Nbe closed, unusable windows are excluded,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.72,0:10:20.62,Default,,0,0,0,,and back-dated forecasts are refused.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.66,0:10:26.74,Default,,0,0,0,,So it's a parameter update, not retraining a neural network\Nafter every meal.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.78,0:10:35.56,Default,,0,0,0,,People differ, so a personal estimate that learns from each\Nperson's own meals is a natural research direction,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.59,0:10:40.16,Default,,0,0,0,,but we haven't shown yet that it beats a population model.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.51,0:10:45.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Every forecast comes with an explanation.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.00,0:10:52.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Here the carbohydrate term contributes about sixty-three\Nmilligrams per decilitre,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.98,0:11:02.14,Default,,0,0,0,,the activity term about minus four, and thirty percent of\Nthe uncertainty is about this person's parameters,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.18,0:11:05.63,Default,,0,0,0,,which shrinks as observations accumulate.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.79,0:11:11.73,Default,,0,0,0,,This toggle shows Model B and Model C for the same meal.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.77,0:11:16.53,Default,,0,0,0,,The research comparison between them was inconclusive,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.58,0:11:21.97,Default,,0,0,0,,so the app shows both side by side and doesn't pick a\Nwinner.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.11,0:11:26.82,Default,,0,0,0,,History lists every forecast with its status,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.85,0:11:34.13,Default,,0,0,0,,and the chart shows beta moving from version zero to version\None while its band narrows,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.17,0:11:37.38,Default,,0,0,0,,so you can audit what changed and when.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.52,0:11:42.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Insights compares forecast with outcome.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.10,0:11:47.61,Default,,0,0,0,,My demonstration outcome of one hundred and eighty-five\Nlanded
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.65,0:11:52.80,Default,,0,0,0,,just outside the first forecast's ninety percent interval,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.84,0:11:55.40,Default,,0,0,0,,and the page says so plainly.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.28,0:12:04.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Finally, persistence. I'll log out and sign back in.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.35,0:12:13.78,Default,,0,0,0,,The twin is still at version one, with its full history.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.82,0:12:20.80,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what makes it a twin rather than a one-off\Nprediction: it keeps a personal state.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.84,0:12:23.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Ownership is checked on every request,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.87,0:12:31.65,Default,,0,0,0,,and the project's eight hundred and fifteen Python tests and\Nthirty-seven frontend tests cover it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.99,0:12:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Now back to the research, because the website demo and the\NCGMacros evaluation are different kinds of evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.04,0:12:48.14,Default,,0,0,0,,The key comparison put Model B against Model C on the same\Nnine
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.18,0:12:53.03,Default,,0,0,0,,hundred and sixty-three meals from thirty-four participants,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.07,0:12:58.33,Default,,0,0,0,,out of fold and sequential, with participant-clustered\Nintervals.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.37,0:13:07.06,Default,,0,0,0,,These numbers come from our recorded runs in the repository\Nreport; they weren't recomputed for this video.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.22,0:13:20.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Model C's area under the curve, which measures how well the\Nmodel ranks risky meals above safe ones,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.33,0:13:24.89,Default,,0,0,0,,was 0.8059 against 0.7943 for Model B.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.93,0:13:33.73,Default,,0,0,0,,The difference, 0.0116, has an interval from minus 0.0084 to\Nplus 0.0479.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.76,0:13:39.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Eight of the nine paired intervals contain zero.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.57,0:13:51.63,Default,,0,0,0,,So it's inconclusive: adding activity hasn't been shown to\Nhelp, and a small effect isn't ruled out.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.82,0:14:00.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Compared with their own never-updated priors, both models\Npoint toward personal updating,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.30,0:14:06.31,Default,,0,0,0,,but no interval excludes zero, so that benefit isn't\Nestablished either.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.36,0:14:13.05,Default,,0,0,0,,The shuffled-history, running-rate and population XGBoost\Ncomparisons are built,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.08,0:14:20.10,Default,,0,0,0,,but there's no real-data run in the repository, so I'm not\Nquoting numbers for them.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.48,0:14:31.94,Default,,0,0,0,,To wrap up. What's new here is the integration: a\Npersistent, versioned twin that forecasts with uncertainty,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.97,0:14:38.38,Default,,0,0,0,,learns from eligible outcomes with a Bayesian update, and\Nexplains itself,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.42,0:14:42.74,Default,,0,0,0,,all tied to a leakage-safe evaluation on CGMacros.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.78,0:14:50.23,Default,,0,0,0,,What the evidence shows is that the Model B versus Model C\Ncomparison is inconclusive,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.27,0:14:54.32,Default,,0,0,0,,and that personalization isn't established yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.48,0:15:03.94,Default,,0,0,0,,The limits: this is an investigational research prototype,\Nnot a medical device and not advice on diet,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.97,0:15:05.75,Default,,0,0,0,,medication or insulin.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.79,0:15:14.33,Default,,0,0,0,,There are only thirty-four participants, the label is a\Nlower bound, and there's no clinical validation.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.37,0:15:19.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Next, we want to run the full key experiment on the real\Ndata,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.48,0:15:24.56,Default,,0,0,0,,and test whether an activity effect differs by activity\Nlevel.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.60,0:15:30.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks for watching. The code is on GitHub at medhachoudhari\Nslash GlycoTwin.
